WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.530
Build multiplication facts from known facts. For example, 6 times 7 equals 5 times 7

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.907
plus 7, so 35 plus 7 equals 42.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:18.509
Use the known fact 8 times 9 equals 72 to find 9 times 9. The answer is 81. Add one

00:00:18.509 --> 00:00:21.599
group of 9: 72 plus 9 equals 81.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:28.333
A learner at a school fair knows 4 times 5 equals 20. How can they calculate 5 times

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:31.602
5 using one more group? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:38.791
A learner at a school fair knows 4 times 5 equals 20. How can they calculate 5 times

00:00:38.791 --> 00:00:45.485
5 using one more group? The answer is 25. Add one group of 5: 20 plus 5 equals 25.
